course: dictionary
lesson: 14164
title: Mitten: a glove with a snug fit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mitten is a kind of glove. It covers your four fingers together in one part, and your thumb has its own separate part. «Ben pulled on his red mittens before he built a snowman.» Snow and snowman are the clues, so a mitten is something you wear to keep your hands warm.
explain: Mittens keep you warmer than gloves in the snow, because your fingers are close together and share the warmth. Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Ben pulled on his red gloves before he built a snowman» still makes sense, so you know the word is about wearing something on your hands.
explain: Mitten has a second meaning. An oven mitt is a thick, padded glove for holding hot pans. «Dad used an oven mitt to lift the hot tray.» The words hot and tray are the clues, so the oven mitt protects his hand from the heat.
explain: In maths, mittens come in pairs, and a pair means two. So 7 pairs of mittens is 14 mittens. Count in twos: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14.
fact: A mitten is a glove with the four fingers together in one part and the thumb in a separate part.
fact: An oven mitt is a thick, padded glove for holding hot pans.
fact: Mittens are warmer than gloves because your fingers stay together.
fact: A pair of mittens means two mittens, one for each hand.
fact: 7 pairs of mittens is 14 mittens.
exercise: «Mia pulled on her warm mittens before she went out in the snow.» What is a mitten? | A pair of shoes for walking | *A glove with the four fingers together in one part | A hat for your head
exercise: «Dad lifted the hot tin with an oven mitt.» What is an oven mitt? | *A thick, padded glove for holding hot pans | A cold drink for summer | A sock for your foot
exercise: There are 7 pairs of mittens. How many mittens are there? | *14 | 12 | 21 | 7
test: «Ella wore her mittens because her fingers were cold.» Why are mittens warm? | They are only worn in summer | They are made of paper | *Their fingers stay together and share the warmth | They have no thumb
test: Sam bought a pair of mittens for the snow. How many mittens is that? | *2 | 4 | 1 | 10
exam: Which word means a thick, padded glove for holding hot pans? | Scarf | Sock | Hat | *Oven mitt
